  "policy": [
    "Normal client bring RPC carries an explicit new_origin bit from the menu NEW selection. The server validates the entire transmitted origin against the current campaign fresh_state, including hero/kit, private party data, empty progress/sequence, purse and initial zone/visit. Only display names are normalized for localization.",
    "Admission applies only to a new participant at gz1g with the initial unnamed party, single authored Human Hero, no other visited or saved zones, no waiting parties/bags, companions/pets, quest journal, quest items or side quests, and no host-load operation in progress.",
    "Every nonexcluded host variable must be one of the six evidenced base startup keys at exactly 1. LiA permits no nonexcluded startup variables. Unknown flags, later values and any advanced/completed quest prevent special admission. This is not a general exclusion of nonquest flags.",
    "Credit the accepted opening vars so subsequent old-value updates align. Normal send_all/package captures the current zone and VM. Preserve the new source hero and purse; never copy the host personal character or inventory.",
    "The existing-reserved-character branch runs before new-origin admission. NEW without acknowledgement cannot replace that participant. Saved origins, missing markers, forged progressed sources and unrelated campaigns retain strict compatibility rules."
  ],
  "fixture_method": [
    "Actual menu keyboard NEW selection and reliable bring/hello/package traffic over local ENet with independent SceneMultiplayer frontends. Host calls normal new_campaign(false), skipping only intro movie playback.",
    "Original opening VM receives 100 native 0.055-second steps. Tests do not seed or copy story flags. In-process fixtures explicitly route the static CampaignState.watch callback to the host, matching separate real processes.",
    "Base uses the opening map's authored bz1g exit record and ordinary Session.leave_zone. LiA dispatches the exact original bz1r LeaveToZone call from parsed script; tutorial movement/combat conditions are not played through. Both peers load the actual first village, then a normal host save emits the returned personal checkpoint.",
    "Four final network cases cover NEW after host initialization and NEW in lobby before Start, in base and LiA. Source hero stats/kit and purse remain their own.",
    "Focused forged-source tests call the tree-bound actual RPC receiver with local sender 0 after validating raw payloads, not a network impersonation test. They cover absent/false/numeric opt-in, changed hero/health/kit/purse/context, story/quests/visits/sequence, wrong campaign and extra state; host-bound checks cover history/body/chapter/items/unknown vars/later values/load. Real positive cases separately exercise the wire path.",
    "Existing divergent-source arrival/re-entry/load guards are rerun unchanged for both campaigns."
  ],
